# systemd presets for policy mode LOCKED.
#
# A preset is a declaration, not an enforcement: it only affects units with no enablement state, and
# only when something runs `systemctl preset`. apply-policy runs the real enable/disable/mask for
# every line below, so the built image carries the state rather than an intention about it. See
# 85-auros-managed.preset for the longer version of this warning.
enable bootc-fetch-apply-updates.timer
disable debug-shell.service
